Asshole.

509
00:32:12.047 --> 00:32:13.796
So tell me, I'm asking you.

510
00:32:13.797 --> 00:32:15.254
"Tell me, I'm asking you."

511
00:32:15.255 --> 00:32:16.754
I told you not to do that.

512
00:32:16.755 --> 00:32:18.254
"Told you not to do that."

513
00:32:18.255 --> 00:32:20.004
Don't fucking play with me right now.

514
00:32:20.005 --> 00:32:22.713
"Don't play with me." Are
you mad? I'm sorry then.

515
00:32:22.714 --> 00:32:23.714
Stop it.

516
00:32:23.715 --> 00:32:26.294
- "Stop it."
- Do it one more time!

517
00:32:26.295 --> 00:32:27.534
"Do it one more time."

518
00:32:27.535 --> 00:32:29.532
I'll do it two more, three more times.

519
00:32:40.047 --> 00:32:43.588
Yoouuu...

520
00:32:43.589 --> 00:32:45.296
Fuuucking...

521
00:32:45.297 --> 00:32:47.855
Assss...

522
00:32:53.797 --> 00:32:56.189
Hooole...

523
00:33:42.912 --> 00:33:44.345
Where...

524
00:33:46.863 --> 00:33:48.088
Am I?

525
00:33:48.821 --> 00:33:52.029
Holy crap! Sis! You're awake!

526
00:33:52.030 --> 00:33:55.279
Sis! Are you okay? Can you
see? Do you recognize me?!

527
00:33:55.280 --> 00:33:57.862
Oh my boy! My boy!

528
00:33:57.863 --> 00:34:01.820
My Jung-yeol, oh my
Jung-yeol! My Jung-yeol!

529
00:34:01.821 --> 00:34:03.154
I need to go get your father!

530
00:34:03.155 --> 00:34:04.695
Mom! Sister's awake!

531
00:34:04.696 --> 00:34:07.445
Keep your eyes open! Keep them open!

532
00:34:07.446 --> 00:34:10.213
Jung-yeol's father! Jung-yeol's father!

533
00:34:28.528 --> 00:34:30.753
So, how many do you see?

534
00:34:31.445 --> 00:34:32.628
Two.

535
00:34:34.070 --> 00:34:37.610
Look here. How many do you see?

536
00:34:37.611 --> 00:34:38.819
Say three. Three.

537
00:34:38.820 --> 00:34:41.961
Shush, seriously.

538
00:34:42.570 --> 00:34:45.718
- Four.
- You got it, four is right. Yes.

539
00:34:46.361 --> 00:34:48.211
Both of them are normal.

540
00:34:49.861 --> 00:34:53.777
As a doctor for over 20 years,
I've never seen anything like this.

541
00:34:53.778 --> 00:34:56.485
It's a miracle, straight
out of a medical drama.

542
00:34:56.486 --> 00:34:58.777
A miracle, truly.

543
00:34:58.778 --> 00:35:01.694
- The car must've been so sturdy, huh?
- Yeah.

544
00:35:01.695 --> 00:35:04.069
- It's because our boy bought it.
- That's right.

545
00:35:04.070 --> 00:35:06.319
Look who bought the house...

546
00:35:06.320 --> 00:35:09.194
We'll keep our eye on their
progress for the next few days.

547
00:35:09.195 --> 00:35:11.319
Thank you so much. That's all we need.

548
00:35:11.320 --> 00:35:13.277
- Just a few more days to recover.
- Thank you, doctor.

549
00:35:13.278 --> 00:35:16.985
Thank you. Oh what a handsome
fella. Thank you so much.

550
00:35:16.986 --> 00:35:17.946
Oh my baby.

551
00:35:17.947 --> 00:35:22.610
Met the wrong woman, had to
bring you back from the gates of hell.

552
00:35:22.611 --> 00:35:24.820
Watch what you say!

553
00:35:25.486 --> 00:35:27.819
Look who's struggling
because of your bum-like son!

554
00:35:27.820 --> 00:35:29.162
"Bum?!"

555
00:35:29.163 --> 00:35:32.610
In-law, relax.

556
00:35:32.611 --> 00:35:35.569
We didn't say he was a bum.
We said he was "bum-like".

557
00:35:35.570 --> 00:35:36.860
Watch it.

558
00:35:36.861 --> 00:35:39.694
This or that, isn't
that the same thing?

559
00:35:39.695 --> 00:35:41.777
Stop trying to spin your words.

560
00:35:41.778 --> 00:35:44.485
You wanna catch some
fists tonight? Huh?!

561
00:35:44.486 --> 00:35:45.711
Excuse me.

562
00:35:46.736 --> 00:35:48.920
Yes? What is it?

563
00:35:49.986 --> 00:35:52.086
I'm sorry as y'all seem busy, but...

564
00:35:53.820 --> 00:35:55.295
Who are y'all?

565
00:35:56.945 --> 00:35:58.860
What's wrong with him.

566
00:35:58.861 --> 00:36:00.985
You got a screw loose?

567
00:36:00.986 --> 00:36:03.610
I thought you fixed your accent 'cause
you didn't wanna sound like a hick.

568
00:36:03.611 --> 00:36:06.295
My child, did you bonk
your head too hard?

569
00:36:06.820 --> 00:36:07.920
Huh?

570
00:36:09.028 --> 00:36:10.628
Hey, is your brain okay?

571
00:36:12.111 --> 00:36:13.537
Na-ra! What's wrong?

572
00:36:13.538 --> 00:36:15.430
I don't know, it's just instinct!

573
00:36:16.911 --> 00:36:18.594
She ain't right either.

574
00:36:19.528 --> 00:36:22.586
It's amnesia, with symptoms
of dissociative identity disorder.

575
00:36:23.185 --> 00:36:24.694
Amnesia...

576
00:36:24.695 --> 00:36:26.277
How do we...

577
00:36:26.278 --> 00:36:28.194
Is my son retarded?

578
00:36:28.195 --> 00:36:29.944
No, he is not.

579
00:36:29.945 --> 00:36:34.027
He won't have any impairment
to his everyday behavior,

580
00:36:34.028 --> 00:36:38.211
but he did lose memory of himself
and the people around him.

581
00:36:39.943 --> 00:36:43.150
You know how it is
in those soap operas.

582
00:36:43.151 --> 00:36:48.025
The protagonist gets in an accident,
loses their memory and wanders about,

583
00:36:48.026 --> 00:36:51.900
then falls in love only to realize that
they were born to a billionaire family,

584
00:36:51.901 --> 00:36:58.734
pitting their deathbed-ridden father
against the poor lover, stuff like that.

585
00:36:58.735 --> 00:37:02.942
Glad they're not long-lost siblings.
You must watch a lot of dramas.

586
00:37:02.943 --> 00:37:07.567
Yes, I even rewatch the great ones on
demand. Imagining that I'm the protagonist.

587
00:37:07.568 --> 00:37:12.025
Then how do we treat them?
Do they need surgery?

588
00:37:12.026 --> 00:37:14.025
Will her memories return?

589
00:37:14.026 --> 00:37:18.668
I suppose another car accident or a timely
bonk to the head will bring them back.

590
00:37:19.360 --> 00:37:20.442
Right, doc?

591
00:37:20.443 --> 00:37:24.251
It's possible. Dramas
aren't all based on fiction.

592
00:37:24.901 --> 00:37:31.960
There was a true case of an American man
who recovered after being hit by a baseball.

593
00:37:33.110 --> 00:37:34.400
We're married?

594
00:37:34.401 --> 00:37:35.650
Married?

595
00:37:35.651 --> 00:37:38.835
Yes. They told me you two were married.

596
00:37:47.193 --> 00:37:48.418
Oh, hi...

597
00:37:50.200 --> 00:37:53.342
<i>Wow, awesome.</i>

598
00:37:54.276 --> 00:37:56.609
<i>I married well.</i>

599
00:37:56.610 --> 00:37:58.001
What the fuck.

600
00:37:58.610 --> 00:37:59.527
Sorry?

601
00:37:59.528 --> 00:38:00.650
Huh?

602
00:38:00.651 --> 00:38:02.317
Did you just curse at me?

603
00:38:02.318 --> 00:38:04.710
I cursed at my past self.

604
00:38:08.818 --> 00:38:10.400
Crazy bitch.

605
00:38:10.401 --> 00:38:12.585
Seriously, crazy bitch.

606
00:38:14.110 --> 00:38:15.418
Wedding picture?

607
00:38:20.110 --> 00:38:22.460
We look good together, huh?

608
00:38:29.401 --> 00:38:30.414
Hmm?

609
00:38:33.318 --> 00:38:34.751
What's this?

610
00:38:40.485 --> 00:38:41.900
- Jung-yeol!
- Jung-yeol!

611
00:38:41.901 --> 00:38:43.025
- Jung-yeol!
- Jung-yeol!

612
00:38:43.026 --> 00:38:43.861
Jung-yeol!

613
00:38:43.862 --> 00:38:46.692
Jung-yeol, speak to me now.

614
00:38:46.693 --> 00:38:48.734
Jung... What the. Oh my gosh!

615
00:38:48.735 --> 00:38:50.442
He's bleeding!

616
00:38:50.443 --> 00:38:51.609
He's bleeding!

617
00:38:51.610 --> 00:38:54.275
See? I told you the rock was too big!

618
00:38:54.276 --> 00:38:59.168
I'm your mother, you see?
Can you remember me?

619
00:38:59.860 --> 00:39:02.234
- You told me you were.
- He's not back.

620
00:39:02.235 --> 00:39:03.775
Oh no, what do we do...

621
00:39:03.776 --> 00:39:07.859
I didn't wanna do it, but your
mother kept forcing me to.

622
00:39:07.860 --> 00:39:09.543
Want me to call the police?

623
00:39:10.318 --> 00:39:12.067
Call what?

624
00:39:12.068 --> 00:39:14.859
No need, I'm his mother.

625
00:39:14.860 --> 00:39:16.859
We're his parents. Father and mother.

626
00:39:16.860 --> 00:39:17.611
Yes.

627
00:39:17.612 --> 00:39:19.025
Domestic violence.

628
00:39:19.026 --> 00:39:20.668
No worries, doc.

629
00:39:21.360 --> 00:39:24.317
I'm alright. No need
to call the police.

630
00:39:24.318 --> 00:39:25.900
It's nothing like that!

631
00:39:25.901 --> 00:39:29.335
- It's just a family tragedy.
- Family, we're family.

632
00:39:40.401 --> 00:39:41.876
Excuse me.

633
00:39:45.091 --> 00:39:46.482
Excuse me.

634
00:39:47.209 --> 00:39:48.468
Huh?

635
00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:55.392
Do you know what the 15th of
next month is supposed to be?

636
00:39:57.125 --> 00:40:00.017
If I remembered, I wouldn't
be laying here right now.

637
00:40:00.667 --> 00:40:02.059
Right.

638
00:40:02.875 --> 00:40:05.975
Uh? You fixed your accent.

639
00:40:07.375 --> 00:40:10.809
I got hit with a rock and passed
out, must've wiped it out of me.

640
00:40:12.417 --> 00:40:17.291
There's an alert set for that
day, so it must be important.

641
00:40:17.292 --> 00:40:18.642
You don't...?

642
00:40:19.542 --> 00:40:21.916
Maybe a wedding
anniversary or something?

643
00:40:21.917 --> 00:40:24.458
Must be your divorce anniversary.

644
00:40:24.459 --> 00:40:25.600
What?

645
00:40:28.691 --> 00:40:30.190
Y'all are getting divorced.

646
00:40:30.191 --> 00:40:31.333
Divorced?

647
00:40:32.900 --> 00:40:34.958
We're getting divorced?

648
00:40:35.691 --> 00:40:38.399
You know, the court gives
you a month to deliberate.

649
00:40:38.400 --> 00:40:40.166
To kill each other during that time.

650
00:40:40.816 --> 00:40:43.208
You should be relieved
for the accident.

651
00:40:44.775 --> 00:40:48.708
If not, one of you would've
killed the other.

652
00:40:49.441 --> 00:40:51.625
No, no way.

653
00:40:52.608 --> 00:40:54.250
It's better than both of you dying.

654
00:40:56.431 --> 00:40:58.357
Why didn't you tell me this earlier?

655
00:40:58.358 --> 00:41:01.833
Who in their right mind would tell
that to someone who almost died...

656
00:41:02.525 --> 00:41:04.166
Why are you speaking down to me?

657
00:41:06.150 --> 00:41:08.750
It's been a few days,
we're acquainted now.

658
00:41:09.983 --> 00:41:12.190
Well, anyways.

659
00:41:12.191 --> 00:41:16.416
Live the rest of your
lives... repenting.

660
00:41:18.316 --> 00:41:19.750
Why?

661
00:41:20.733 --> 00:41:22.375
They're free to leave tomorrow.

662
00:41:25.901 --> 00:41:29.607
That's great news, I won't
need to see her anymore.

663
00:41:29.608 --> 00:41:35.107
Please watch over my daughter-in...
I mean, this lady's daughter.

664
00:41:35.108 --> 00:41:36.774
Take care of her, please.

665
00:41:36.775 --> 00:41:41.041
I wish good health
for your son as well.

666
00:41:41.733 --> 00:41:42.733
Okay.

667
00:41:42.734 --> 00:41:46.500
But why are you trying to
split up the married couple?

668
00:41:50.608 --> 00:41:54.149
I'm just offering my
opinion as a doctor.

669
00:41:54.150 --> 00:41:57.107
Living in the same environment
from before the accident

670
00:41:57.108 --> 00:42:00.034
will help greatly in
recovering their memories.

671
00:42:00.035 --> 00:42:05.176
A new environment will stimulate their
brain less, and delay their recovery.

672
00:42:06.483 --> 00:42:08.117
Hey, in-law.

673
00:42:08.118 --> 00:42:09.551
What?

674
00:42:12.717 --> 00:42:15.815
As the doctor suggested,

675
00:42:15.816 --> 00:42:21.041
why don't we keep them together
until their divorce is final?

676
00:42:23.025 --> 00:42:24.607
I don't think so.

677
00:42:24.608 --> 00:42:27.625
Our kids can't even
remember who they are.

678
00:42:28.233 --> 00:42:32.250
Isn't it a parent's duty, to try
to help in any way we can?

679
00:42:35.404 --> 00:42:40.441
It kills me that they can't even
remember their own parents.

680
00:42:40.442 --> 00:42:44.572
But what'll we do if they
fall in love all over again?

681
00:42:44.573 --> 00:42:47.156
If you have any ulterior
motives, don't even try me.

682
00:42:47.157 --> 00:42:50.382
I can see clearly where
my Jung-yeol stands now.

683
00:42:51.272 --> 00:42:53.822
I can say the same for you.

684
00:42:53.823 --> 00:42:57.697
When the divorce is done, I'm
sending Na-ra to study overseas.

685
00:42:57.698 --> 00:42:59.906
That's welcome news.

686
00:42:59.907 --> 00:43:03.822
I was worried your daughter
might come crying back.

687
00:43:03.823 --> 00:43:06.364
Mmm. Sounds like
something your son might pull.

688
00:43:06.365 --> 00:43:09.447
Never! He's the winner in this.

689
00:43:09.448 --> 00:43:14.624
Divorce is but a scratch these days,
he'll brush it off and start anew.

690
00:43:14.625 --> 00:43:18.142
Then you agree with me on this.

691
00:43:18.782 --> 00:43:20.041
Agree on what?

692
00:43:20.042 --> 00:43:26.558
To try to recover their memories,
but to make sure they get divorced.

693
00:43:29.615 --> 00:43:32.298
No way! No way in hell!

694
00:43:33.032 --> 00:43:37.406
Am I some servant? Why do
I have to watch those idiots?!

695
00:43:37.407 --> 00:43:40.197
Because she's your older sister.

696
00:43:40.198 --> 00:43:45.173
She's your daughter,
you go ahead and do it.

697
00:43:48.115 --> 00:43:54.531
I'm not telling you to bathe
her. Just stick by her side.

698
00:43:54.532 --> 00:43:57.382
Can't we just stick them in an asylum?

699
00:43:59.865 --> 00:44:02.322
What if they smear shit on the wall?

700
00:44:02.323 --> 00:44:03.715
Hey.

701
00:44:05.073 --> 00:44:06.757
I can hear you.

702
00:44:08.323 --> 00:44:11.340
Yes, it's a little rude
with us sitting right here.

703
00:44:13.907 --> 00:44:17.322
Hey lady... I mean, mother.

704
00:44:17.323 --> 00:44:23.656
I don't like this either. Do I
have to live with this man?

705
00:44:23.657 --> 00:44:29.173
He's not my style, and what if
he tries to force himself on me?

706
00:44:30.573 --> 00:44:32.757
You two are definitely sisters.

707
00:44:34.580 --> 00:44:36.514
Both families agreed to this.

708
00:44:37.463 --> 00:44:39.438
Just do as you're told.

709
00:44:47.455 --> 00:44:50.847
How fortunate that I know the passcode.

710
00:44:56.612 --> 00:44:59.413
Is this a home for a human?

711
00:44:59.414 --> 00:45:02.163
Oh the smell, it reeks.

712
00:45:02.164 --> 00:45:04.829
Is there a dead body somewhere?

713
00:45:04.830 --> 00:45:07.722
This can't be a kitchen.

714
00:45:09.376 --> 00:45:10.768
Let me take a look.

715
00:45:13.747 --> 00:45:15.413
Thank goodness there are no bodies.

716
00:45:15.414 --> 00:45:20.371
With the husband drinking
this much, no wonder...

717
00:45:20.372 --> 00:45:22.639
Mmm, that's all you.

718
00:45:23.872 --> 00:45:29.163
How hard did he make my life,
causing me to drink this much.

719
00:45:29.164 --> 00:45:31.722
Might as well buy a new house.

720
00:45:34.789 --> 00:45:39.496
I can feel in these photos...

721
00:45:39.497 --> 00:45:41.805
murderous intent.

722
00:45:42.455 --> 00:45:43.805
Yup.

723
00:45:44.747 --> 00:45:46.014
Sorry.

724
00:45:54.672 --> 00:45:57.730
<i>Wanna watch baseball
together next time?</i>

725
00:46:06.580 --> 00:46:08.389
Ah, what the hell is this?

726
00:46:09.164 --> 00:46:12.597
Ouch. What do you want?

727
00:46:15.789 --> 00:46:18.246
You have to stay vigilant out there.

728
00:46:18.247 --> 00:46:19.247
"Vigilant?"

729
00:46:19.248 --> 00:46:22.871
Watch over them, so they
don't fall back in love.

730
00:46:22.872 --> 00:46:25.496
I don't want to! You do it!

731
00:46:25.497 --> 00:46:29.121
I can't stay here all day.
What about Dad?

732
00:46:29.122 --> 00:46:32.496
I don't want to. I can't.

733
00:46:32.497 --> 00:46:35.139
I have to start preparing
for auditions.

734
00:46:35.914 --> 00:46:38.663
Ugh... Are you gonna keep doing that?

735
00:46:38.664 --> 00:46:42.430
No, I'm gonna keep doing thiiis!

736
00:46:51.497 --> 00:46:55.097
Please, mother. I must've been crazy.

737
00:46:56.837 --> 00:47:00.687
Rest up after you finish cleaning. We
have an important meeting tomorrow.

738
00:47:03.046 --> 00:47:04.521
You two.

739
00:47:05.587 --> 00:47:07.937
Don't forget that you're
getting divorced.

740
00:47:13.754 --> 00:47:15.062
Bye...

741
00:47:19.337 --> 00:47:22.878
No. Over here. Not there.
Don't you see the dust?

742
00:47:22.879 --> 00:47:26.878
No, a little more. No,
no, right next to you.

743
00:47:26.879 --> 00:47:30.253
Why can't you see it? It's right there.

744
00:47:30.254 --> 00:47:33.878
No, the dust is here. Clean this.

745
00:47:33.879 --> 00:47:35.170
No, here!

746
00:47:35.171 --> 00:47:38.920
Hey! Why aren't you cleaning?

747
00:47:38.921 --> 00:47:40.354
I am, with my mouth.

748
00:47:41.671 --> 00:47:45.753
Hey! I told you to
clean the sofa first.

749
00:47:45.754 --> 00:47:47.271
Sheesh...

750
00:47:54.754 --> 00:47:57.562
You're back from the
dead. Have a drink.

751
00:47:58.969 --> 00:48:00.569
Was it you who was hospitalized?

752
00:48:03.087 --> 00:48:09.172
What the... Why is the stench of
my dad piercing through my pork?

753
00:48:09.712 --> 00:48:11.062
Oh.

754
00:48:13.629 --> 00:48:17.104
After my shower, I
applied a bit of toner.

755
00:48:23.421 --> 00:48:27.604
Why do you smell like such
an old dude? Didn't it sting?

756
00:48:28.254 --> 00:48:29.521
Not my face.

757
00:48:31.212 --> 00:48:33.420
How did you live for
years with this smell?

758
00:48:33.421 --> 00:48:35.854
I mean, I guess you don't even wash.

759
00:48:37.754 --> 00:48:40.312
Miss Na-ra, why did you do that?

760
00:48:42.436 --> 00:48:44.852
My hand just did it by itself.

761
00:48:44.853 --> 00:48:48.394
Why'd you hit her so
hard? Are you alright?

762
00:48:48.395 --> 00:48:49.364
What?

763
00:48:49.365 --> 00:48:51.435
With the chicken leg, she...

764
00:48:51.436 --> 00:48:53.911
